## Cache Invalidation Strategies

- **Explicit invalidation**: Proactively delete cache keys when data changes
- **TTL-based**: Allow cache entries to expire naturally based on time-to-live
- **Write-through**: Update both cache and database simultaneously

## Implementation

```javascript
// Cache-aside with explicit invalidation
async function updateProfile(userId, data) {
  await redis.del(`user:${userId}`);
  await db.users.update(userId, data);
  return await getUserProfile(userId);
}
```

## Trade-offs

- **Explicit invalidation**: Provides immediate consistency but requires additional coordination
- **TTL-based**: Simpler to implement with eventual consistency guarantees
- **Write-through**: Optimal for read-heavy workloads but can increase write latency

## Why This Is Asked
This tests understanding of a practical CQRS+ES saga across services, including event modeling, simple orchestration, and read-model convergence. It also probes idempotency, compensation, and basic testing concerns.

## Key Concepts
- Event types: RoomBooked, RoomReserved, RoomReleased, BookingCancelled
- Projections: BookingReadModel, AvailabilityReadModel
- Saga/coordinator: orchestrated flow with simple compensation
- Idempotency and exactly-once handling in event handlers
- Testing: simulate failure, ensure eventual consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
class EventStore {
  async append(streamId, events) {
    // Append events to stream with optimistic concurrency
  }

  async getEvents(streamId) {
    // Retrieve events for projections
  }
}

class BookingSaga {
  async handleRoomBooked(event) {
    try {
      await this.availabilityService.reserveRoom(event.data);
      this.emit('RoomReserved', event.data);
    } catch (error) {
      this.emit('BookingCancelled', event.data);
      this.emit('RoomReleased', event.data);
    }
  }
}

// Projection for read model
class BookingProjection {
  async handle(event) {
    switch (event.type) {
      case 'RoomBooked':
        await this.updateBookingStatus(event.data.bookingId, 'pending');
        break;
      case 'BookingCancelled':
        await this.updateBookingStatus(event.data.bookingId, 'cancelled');
        break;
    }
  }
}
```

